{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2963","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2963","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2963\",\"parent_revision\":\"33f269674ed42c3970012fff0331e7e1b896a5bf\",\"root_revision\":\"c3e17b10c116799ef94b41d6ba045e3cf346ebf97830362b7cb8de4b4eb2acd6\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-18\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nOriginal observation (from #2956, a different diagnosis session, 2026-08-18): across several consecutive backlog_groom writes on real GitHub-backend items (#2953, #2955), the response line \\\"Reconciled #N: X provider patch(es), Y pending mutation(s), 0 failures\\\" showed Y draining very slowly (29 -> 27) and never reaching 0, meaning previously-queued mutations to the linked GitHub issue's body never actually land on GitHub even though the tool reports success.\\n\\nConfirmed distinct from #2956 (verified 2026-08-18 while fixing #2956): #2956's root cause is pure section-key normalization logic (operations.py/github_sync.py/rendering.py/parsing.py) with no network or sync dependency; the pending-mutation queue lives in a completely separate subsystem (backend.reconcile(), FileCache, and the GraphQL issue-update path in github_backend.py). The #2956 fix does not touch any of those files, so it cannot affect this symptom either way.\\n\\nAlso confirmed NOT the same mechanism as #2907 (\\\"artifact/plan content writes never land \u2014 GitHub ruleset blocks direct Contents API commits to main\\\"): #2907 is specifically about GitHubBackend.put_content() (artifact manifests, plans) using the Contents API. backlog_groom's issue-body updates go through a different mechanism (GraphQL updateIssue via the SyncProvider.reconcile() path in github_backend.py), so #2907's branch-protection-on-Contents-API root cause does not directly explain this symptom \u2014 needs its own trace.\\n\\n**Research first**: confirm live whether GITHUB_TOKEN reaches the actual write attempt during this flow (this investigator's own fastmcp-based reproduction attempt hit an unrelated environment confound \u2014 GITHUB_TOKEN not forwarded into the fastmcp subprocess \u2014 so any repro must first rule that out, per reproduction-integrity discipline, before concluding the mutation queue itself is broken). Trace github_backend.py's reconcile()/GraphQL update path and FileCache's pending-mutation replay logic for why a queued mutation can survive a \\\"0 failures\\\" reconcile report without landing on GitHub. Related: #2956, #2903, #2907.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **github-backend issue-body reconcile: pending mutations accumulate and never drain across grooming sessions** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input, split out of #2956\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c3abd20c01ef120df0538a4cf609343f7163a9ec80a562ab30c0bb13878bbea8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgwRTQ\"}"}